9846862827476702], [[[179.0, 1028.0], [1286.0, 1026.0], [1286.0, 1056.0], [179.0, 1058.0]], 'too large. A point estimate and 95% confidence interval for the adjusted relative risk will be', 0.9895909644187765], [[[181.0, 1063.0], [520.0, 1062.0], [520.0, 1092.0], [181.0, 1093.0]], 'reported for the final model.', 0.9889649707695534], [[[180.0, 1127.0], [570.0, 1128.0], [570.0, 1158.0], [180.0, 1157.0]], '9.4.3Impact of Missing Data', 0.9820385376612345], [[[180.0, 1225.0], [1331.0, 1227.0], [1331.0, 1256.0], [180.0, 1254.0]], 'will be conducted to assess the impact of missing data assumptions and handling on the primary', 0.9883358472205223], [[[179.0, 1258.0], [1306.0, 1259.0], [1306.0, 1292.0], [179.0, 1291.0]], 'study inference. This analysis will be conducted if the amount of missing data for the primary', 0.9984860299749577], [[[180.0, 1294.0], [1354.0, 1294.0], [1354.0, 1326.0], [180.0, 1326.0]], 'endpoint exceeds 5%. Multiple imputed datasets will be generated from an imputation model that', 0.9845546078174672], [[[178.0, 1327.0], [1312.0, 1328.0], [1312.0, 1361.0], [178.0, 1360.0]], 'includes the explanatory variables from the primary analysis, in addition to ancillary variables', 0.9861043331523737], [[[178.0, 1363.0], [1316.0, 1363.0], [1316.0, 1396.0], [178.0, 1396.0]], 'that are thought to explain the missingness or predict mortality or BPD at 36 weeks PMA. The', 0.9873152582541757], [[[176.0, 1396.0], [1339.0, 1397.0], [1339.0, 1430.0], [176.0, 1429.0]], 'number of data sets imputed will be equal to 1o0 times the fraction of missing outcome data (i.e.', 0.9844797585428375], [[[177.0, 1432.0], [1238.0, 1432.0], [1238.0, 1465.0], [177.0, 1465.0]], 'if 25% of infants are missing the primary outcome, 25 data sets will be imputed), with a', 0.9860934161327102], [[[178.0, 1498.0], [1257.0, 1502.0], [1257.0, 1535.0], [178.0, 1531.0]], 'statistical methods described in Section 9.3, and parameter estimates will be pooled using', 0.9932910720507304], [[[178.0, 1536.0], [1345.0, 1536.0], [1345.0, 1568.0], [178.0, 1568.0]], "Rubin's combination rules to produce estimates and standard errors that incorporate missing data", 0.9981801491230726], [[[179.0, 1606.0], [1344.0, 1606.0], [1344.0, 1635.0], [179.0, 1635.0]], 'random (MAR) and provides an evaluation of impact of missing data uncertainty. Therefore, due', 0.9866293252155345], [[[176.0, 1638.0], [1261.0, 1639.0], [1261.0, 1672.0], [176.0, 1671.0]], 'to the utilization of generalized estimating equation methods for the primary analysis, this', 0.9952437171469564], [[[180.0, 1676.0], [1289.0, 1676.0], [1289.0, 1705.0], [180.0, 1705.0]], 'sensitivity analysis is namely evaluating the robustness of the primary analysis to departures', 0.9981012223882878], [[[178.0, 1708.0], [1348.0, 1708.0], [1348.0, 1743.0], [178.0, 1743.0]], '   a   ss si  d n n  n ', 0.6129169651995534], [[[180.0, 1836.0], [379.0, 1836.0], [379.0, 1862.0], [180.0, 1862.0]], 'Version 1.3,2024-09-10', 0.9952985806898638], [[[1284.0, 1836.0], [1353.0, 1836.0], [1353.0, 1864.0], [1284.0, 1864.0]], 'Page 31', 0.998872527054378]]
